### Pruebas del módulo Employees — POST /employees · GET /employees
### Prerrequisito: servidor corriendo con `npm run start:dev` y migración aplicada

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000

# Pega aquí los tokens después de ejecutar los logins de la sección 1
@ownerToken   = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOjEsInVzZXJuYW1lIjoiYWRtaW4xMjMiLCJyb2xlIjoiT1dORVIiLCJpYXQiOjE3Nzk0NjUwNDksImV4cCI6MTc3OTUwODI0OX0.Qpnl5UsJ_z25F4eQ8II3DBlNWbS0PvC6xQRMAj94t9Y
@managerToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJzdWIiOjIsInVzZXJuYW1lIjoiY2FybG9zLmdlcmVudGUiLCJyb2xlIjoiTUFOQUdFUiIsImlhdCI6MTc3OTQ2NTI4NCwiZXhwIjoxNzc5NTA4NDg0fQ._f7SE3aZck3MiDnfIJiaMolmK4VgRI4d7Bn-DYwOobE

### =============================================================
### 1. LOGIN — obtención de tokens
### =============================================================

### 1A. Login como OWNER → copia el access_token y pégalo en @ownerToken
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin123",
  "password": "supersecretpassword"
}

### 1B. Login como el Manager creado en 2A → copia el token y pégalo en @managerToken
###     (ejecutar DESPUÉS del paso 2A)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "carlos.gerente",
  "password": "gerente1234"
}

### =============================================================
### 2. OWNER crea empleados — casos de éxito
### =============================================================

### 2A. OWNER crea un MANAGER (cargo "Manager" → role MANAGER automático)
###     Debe responder 201 con el perfil completo sin password
POST {{baseUrl}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "carlos.gerente",
  "password": "gerente1234",
  "dni": "74839201",
  "nombres": "Carlos",
  "apellidoPaterno": "Mendoza",
  "apellidoMaterno": "Rios",
  "fechaNacimiento": "1990-03-15",
  "cargo": "Manager",
  "turno": "MAÑANA",
  "fechaInicio": "2026-01-10",
  "telefono": "987654321",
  "email": "carlos.mendoza@lumina.pe"
}

### 2B. OWNER crea un EMPLOYEE con cargo "Recepcionista"
###     Debe responder 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "lucia.recepcion",
  "password": "recep5678",
  "dni": "76543210",
  "nombres": "Lucía",
  "apellidoPaterno": "Torres",
  "apellidoMaterno": "Vega",
  "fechaNacimiento": "1998-07-22",
  "cargo": "Recepcionista",
  "turno": "TARDE",
  "fechaInicio": "2026-02-01",
  "telefono": "912345678",
  "email": "lucia.torres@lumina.pe"
}

### 2C. OWNER crea un EMPLOYEE con cargo "Limpieza"
###     Debe responder 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "jose.limpieza",
  "password": "limpieza999",
  "dni": "68901234",
  "nombres": "José",
  "apellidoPaterno": "Quispe",
  "apellidoMaterno": "Mamani",
  "fechaNacimiento": "1995-11-08",
  "cargo": "Limpieza",
  "turno": "NOCHE",
  "fechaInicio": "2026-03-05",
  "telefono": "956789012",
  "email": "jose.quispe@lumina.pe",
  "direccion": "Av. Los Pinos 342, Miraflores"
}

### =============================================================
### 3. MANAGER crea empleados — jerarquía
### =============================================================

### 3A. MANAGER crea un EMPLOYEE con cargo "Botones" (Debe funcionar)
###     Prerrequisito: @managerToken cargado (paso 1B)
POST {{baseUrl}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "pedro.botones",
  "password": "botones321",
  "dni": "72345678",
  "nombres": "Pedro",
  "apellidoPaterno": "Huanca",
  "apellidoMaterno": "Lima",
  "fechaNacimiento": "2000-05-19",
  "cargo": "Botones",
  "turno": "MAÑANA",
  "fechaInicio": "2026-04-01",
  "telefono": "934567890",
  "email": "pedro.huanca@lumina.pe"
}

### 3B. MANAGER intenta crear otro MANAGER (Debe fallar — 409 Conflict)
###     "Los Managers solo pueden crear Empleados"
POST {{baseUrl}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "ana.gerente",
  "password": "gerente9999",
  "dni": "79999999",
  "nombres": "Ana",
  "apellidoPaterno": "Flores",
  "apellidoMaterno": "Cruz",
  "fechaNacimiento": "1988-02-14",
  "cargo": "Manager",
  "turno": "TARDE",
  "fechaInicio": "2026-04-01",
  "telefono": "999888777",
  "email": "ana.flores@lumina.pe"
}

### =============================================================
### 4. Conflictos — unicidad de datos
### =============================================================

### 4A. Username duplicado (Debe fallar — 409 "El nombre de usuario ya está en uso")
POST {{baseUrl}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "carlos.gerente",
  "password": "otrapass123",
  "dni": "11111111",
  "nombres": "Otro",
  "apellidoPaterno": "Apellido",
  "apellidoMaterno": "Dos",
  "fechaNacimiento": "1991-01-01",
  "cargo": "Recepcionista",
  "turno": "MAÑANA",
  "fechaInicio": "2026-05-01",
  "telefono": "911111111",
  "email": "otro.email@lumina.pe"
}

### 4B. DNI duplicado (Debe fallar — 409 "El DNI ya está registrado")
POST {{baseUrl}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "nuevo.usuario",
  "password": "otrapass123",
  "dni": "74839201",
  "nombres": "Nuevo",
  "apellidoPaterno": "Usuario",
  "apellidoMaterno": "Test",
  "fechaNacimiento": "1992-06-15",
  "cargo": "Botones",
  "turno": "TARDE",
  "fechaInicio": "2026-05-01",
  "telefono": "922222222",
  "email": "nuevo.usuario@lumina.pe"
}

### 4C. Email duplicado (Debe fallar — 409 "El correo electrónico ya está registrado")
POST {{baseUrl}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "otro.usuario",
  "password": "otrapass123",
  "dni": "22222222",
  "nombres": "Otro",
  "apellidoPaterno": "Usuario",
  "apellidoMaterno": "Bis",
  "fechaNacimiento": "1993-09-20",
  "cargo": "Limpieza",
  "turno": "NOCHE",
  "fechaInicio": "2026-05-01",
  "telefono": "933333333",
  "email": "carlos.mendoza@lumina.pe"
}

### =============================================================
### 5. Seguridad / validación
### =============================================================

### 5A. Sin token (Debe fallar — 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/employees
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "intruso",
  "password": "hack12345",
  "dni": "99999999",
  "nombres": "Intruso",
  "apellidoPaterno": "Test",
  "apellidoMaterno": "Test",
  "fechaNacimiento": "1990-01-01",
  "cargo": "Botones",
  "turno": "MAÑANA",
  "fechaInicio": "2026-05-01",
  "telefono": "900000000",
  "email": "intruso@hack.com"
}

### 5B. Payload incompleto — falta dni y email (Debe fallar — 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "incompleto",
  "password": "pass12345",
  "nombres": "Sin",
  "apellidoPaterno": "Datos",
  "apellidoMaterno": "Completos",
  "fechaNacimiento": "1990-01-01",
  "cargo": "Botones",
  "turno": "TARDE",
  "fechaInicio": "2026-05-01",
  "telefono": "900000001"
}

### =============================================================
### 6. GET /employees — lectura de la lista
### =============================================================

### 6A. OWNER lista todos (Debe devolver todos los empleados incluyendo el propio OWNER)
GET {{baseUrl}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{ownerToken}}

### 6B. MANAGER lista empleados (Debe devolver todos EXCEPTO el OWNER)
GET {{baseUrl}}/employees
Authorization: Bearer {{managerToken}}
